{
  "id": "coulomb_s_law",
  "title": "Coulomb's Law",
  "description": "Calculate the electric force acting between two point charges using Coulomb's Law. The electric force is determined by the charges and the distance between them.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Coulomb's Law\n\nCoulomb's law calculates the electric force acting between two electric charges *q1* and *q2*:\n\n**F = k q1 q2 / r²**\n\nWhere:\n- **F** = force of attraction or repulsion (N)\n- **k** = Coulomb's constant = 8.9875517873681764 × 10⁹ (Nm²/C²)\n- **q1, q2** = charges (Coulombs, C)\n- **r** = distance between charges (m)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "q1",
          "label": "Charge 1 (q1)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "C",
          "defaultValue": 0.000002
        },
        {
          "id": "q2",
          "label": "Charge 2 (q2)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "C",
          "defaultValue": 0.000002
        },
        {
          "id": "r",
          "label": "Distance between charges (r)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 0.02
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "force",
          "label": "Electric Force",
          "unit": "N",
          "formula": "(8.9875517873681764e9 * inputs.q1 * inputs.q2) / (inputs.r * inputs.r)",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Charge 1 (C)",
        "Charge 2 (C)",
        "Distance (m)",
        "Force (N)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          0.000001,
          0.000001,
          0.01,
          8.987551787368176
        ],
        [
